=== vocabulary ===
A policy is a kind of policy.
A role is a kind of role.
A credential is a kind of credential.
A verdict is a kind of verdict.
An allowlist entry is a kind of fact.
A resource is a kind of resource.
An environment is a kind of environment.
An access request is a kind of process.
A user is a kind of person.
A reviewer is a kind of person.
A security officer is a kind of person.

A policy has a name, a status, and a version.
A role has a name and a status.
A credential has an owner, a status, a rotated at, a use count, and a use limit.
A verdict has a subject, an outcome, and a decided at.
An allowlist entry has a user id and a resource name.
A resource has a name, a classification, and a status.
An environment has a name and a status.
An access request has a number, a requestor, a resource name, a status, a requested at, and a queue position.
An access request can be pending or approved or denied or granted, called the request status.
A user has a user id, a name, a role, a clearance, and a status.
A reviewer has a user id and a name.
A security officer has a user id and a name.

A resource is keyed by the name.

Definition: a resource is classified if its classification is "classified".
Definition: a user is cleared if its clearance is "granted".
Definition: a user is privileged if its role is "admin".
Definition: a user is authorized if it is cleared and it is privileged.
Definition: a credential is overused if its use count is more than its use limit.
Definition: a credential is fresh if its rotated at is within the last 90 days.
Definition: an access request is stale if its requested at is within the last 7 days.
Definition: an access request is pending if its status is "pending".

Assignment relates a user to a role.
Assignment is read via the policy.evaluate tool.
Grant relates a user to a resource.
Grant is read via the access.grant tool.
Coverage relates a policy to an environment.
Coverage is read via the policy.evaluate tool.

The verb to authorize (it authorizes, it is authorized) means the assignment relation.
The verb to grant (it grants, it is granted) means the grant relation.
The verb to cover (it covers, it is covered) means the coverage relation.

To fetch pending access requests:
  bind access requests = invoke request.list with status = "pending".

To fetch active credentials:
  bind credentials = invoke request.list with status = "active".

To grant access to a resource for a user:
  invoke access.grant with user = the user, resource = the resource.

To revoke access to a resource for a user:
  invoke access.revoke with user = the user, resource = the resource.

To revoke an access request:
  invoke access.revoke with user = the access request's requestor, resource = the access request's resource name.

To rotate a credential:
  invoke credential.rotate with credential = the credential.

To log an audit entry for an access request:
  invoke audit.log with request = the access request.

To evaluate the policy for an environment:
  bind verdict = invoke policy.evaluate with environment = the environment.

To escalate an access request:
  invoke audit.log with request = the access request.

=== constants ===

The max concurrent grants is 3.
The credential ttl is 90 days.
The review window is 7 days.

=== instances ===

There is an environment called identity provider:
  name = "okta"
  status = "active"

There is an environment called audit sink:
  name = "audit-log"
  status = "active"

=== language ===
Comparison synonyms:
  outranks = is more than
  lacks = is less than
  matches = is
Duration synonyms:
  rotation window = 90 days
Assertion synonyms:
  confirm
  ensure

=== trace ===
retention: 30 days
sample floor: 5
default monitor cadence: 7 days
profile: production

=== tools ===
List Access Requests
=====================
-- List access requests by status.
~ request.list(status: String) : List
  capture: hash-only

Grant Access
============
-- Grant access to a resource for a user.
~ access.grant(user: User, resource: Resource) : Boolean
  capture: hash-only

Revoke Access
=============
-- Revoke access to a resource for a user.
~ access.revoke(user: User, resource: Resource) : Boolean
  capture: hash-only

Rotate Credential
=================
-- Rotate a credential.
~ credential.rotate(credential: Credential) : Boolean
  capture: hash-only

Log Audit Entry
===============
-- Log an audit entry for an access request.
~ audit.log(request: AccessRequest) : Boolean
  capture: hash-only

Evaluate Policy
===============
-- Evaluate the policy for an environment.
~ policy.evaluate(environment: Environment) : Verdict
  capture: hash-only
